# Blood Sun: "When this enchantment enters, draw a card. All lands lose all abilities except mana abilities."
# - The draw (CR 603.6a): Bot1's hand is 4 once Blood Sun is cast and 5 once its trigger resolves.
# - Mutavault keeps "{T}: Add {C}", a mana ability (CR 605.1a), and loses "{1}: ... becomes a 2/2", which costs mana but
#   adds none (the ruling: a mana ability produces mana). Bot1 animates it on turn 1, before the Sun (the positive control),
#   and cannot on turn 3, after it; it still taps for {C}.
# - Bot2's Azorius Chancery is the positive control on turn 2: it enters tapped and its trigger returns it. Under the Sun,
#   on turn 4, its "enters tapped" and its "when this land enters" are lost before they can apply (the rulings; CR 614.12:
#   a permanent entering is judged as it would exist on the battlefield): it enters untapped, nothing triggers, and it keeps
#   "{T}: Add {W}{U}" and taps for it. It is still a Land with no land type: Blood Sun changes no type.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mutavault
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Blood Sun
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Azorius Chancery
Island x30

